Some of the biggest writers in television shared an insight into their processes during Variety’s annual Night in the Writers’ Room on November 11. For the “Awards Season Edition,” scribes behind top comedies, drama and limited series detailed their very different experiences of creating hit shows — whether new series like “The Greatest” and “Dig” or those wrapping up like “The Comeback.”

Creator, showrunner, executive producer, director, writer &ldquo;P-Valley&rdquo;

&ldquo;I care about the story being the best it can be. I care about your perspective. I want to hear eerything that everyone has to say, and so my room is very democratic &mdash; literally everyone has equal say.&rdquo;

The awards season acting races are taking shape, and nothing will test them like the Actor Awards , the ceremony formerly known as the SAG Awards. There is a real possibility the season is barreling toward another edition of #OscarsSoWhite, and this is the stage where the nominating committee can exert the most influence. In TV, a similar problem remains after an Emmys full of white winners. With first-time contenders, overdue veterans and potential breakout performances crowding every category, nothing is locked. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Jane Fonda 'Didn't Dare Imagine' Democrats' Blue Tsunami: 'We Have to Block What's Bad and Fight For What's Good' ‘Artificial’ Star Andrew Garfield Recalls Believing OpenAI’s Sam Altman Was ‘Genuinely Great’ and Could Be ‘My Future Best Friend’

Andrew Scott has three Actor Award nominations from his TV work, but none for film &#x2014; Focus Features&#x2019; &#x201C;Elsinore&#x201D; could finally give SAG voters a chance to catch up with what theater audiences have known for years. John Malkovich, who has two Actor Awards nominations &#x2014; the latest one for ensemble cast in 2000 &#x2014; is close behind for Martin McDonagh&#x2019;s &#x201C;Wild Horse Nine.&#x201D; Matt Damon, carrying Christopher Nolan&#x2019;s &#x201C;The Odyssey,&#x201D; has seven Actor prize nominations but is looking for that first win. Ryan Gosling&#x2019;s everyman science teacher turned hero in &#x201C;Project Hail Mary&#x201D; has emerged as one of the race&#x2019;s most beloved performances and could hand the six-time nominee another bid. John Turturro rounds out the category for the indie drama &#x201C;The Only Living Pickpocket in New York.&#x201D; The veteran actor has six Actor Award noms, but only one for a feature film. Pedro Pascal (&#x201C;Behemoth!&#x201D;) and newcomer Anthony Ippolito (&#x201C;I Play Rocky&#x201D;) are potential entrants, along with Jaafar Jackson (&#x201C;Michael&#x201D;) and Sebastian Stan (&#x201C;Fjord&#x201D;). blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Julianne Moore is back in the conversation more than a decade after winning for &#x201C;Still Alice.&#x201D; Her performance in Jesse Eisenberg&#x2019;s &#x201C;The Debut&#x201D; anchors a film that is also gaining traction in other categories across all awards, including Oscar. This combination could make it difficult to unseat her as the favorite.

The season&#x2019;s breakout is Inde Navarrette, whose work in the horror film &#x201C;Obsession&#x201D; has turned a festival discovery into a serious top-five contender. Olivia Wilde is also in the mix for &#x201C;The Invite,&#x201D; which she also directed, giving her awards season narrative a boost. Voters have rarely been inclusive of non-English-language performances, which leaves Sandra H&#xFC;ller from &#x201C;Rose&#x201D; &#x2014; and others like Virginie Efira (&#x201C;All of a Sudden&#x201D;) &#x2014; vulnerable to a snub.

The nominating committee loves Emily Blunt, which could carry her into the fold for Steven Spielberg&#x2019;s &#x201C;Disclosure Day.&#x201D; She&#x2019;s landed noms for her wide range of work, including &#x201C;The Girl on the Train,&#x201D; &#x201C;Mary Poppins Returns,&#x201D; &#x201C;A Quiet Place&#x201D; and &#x201C;Oppenheimer.&#x201D; She even won for the latter two, making her one of only two performers to turn a SAG film-acting win into nothing at the Academy, the other being Idris Elba for &#x201C;Beasts of No Nation.&#x201D;

Zendaya has two possible entries &#x2014; &#x201C;Dune: Part Three&#x201D; and &#x201C;The Drama&#x201D; &#x2014; testing her ability to avoid a vote split.

Andrew Garfield leads for his portrayal of OpenAI chief Sam Altman in Luca Guadagnino&#x2019;s &#x201C;Artificial.&#x201D; A three-time nominee playing one of the decade&#x2019;s most scrutinized figures makes for a compelling awards combination.

John Leguizamo could earn his first nomination for &#x201C;The Odyssey,&#x201D; delivering a performance that&#x2019;s the moral center of Nolan&#x2019;s epic. Paul Giamatti (&#x201C;The Debut&#x201D;) and Sam Rockwell (&#x201C;Wild Horse Nine&#x201D;) are familiar faces the guild knows well. The last slot could go to Guitarricadelafuente, whose feature film debut in Netflix&#x2019;s Spanish-language &#x201C;La Bola Negra&#x201D; has made him one of the season&#x2019;s most intriguing newcomers, but again, non-English-language performances struggle here. Still, Netflix got the &#x201C;Emilia P&#xE9;rez&#x201D; stars there, with a win for Zoe Salda&#xF1;a. Colman Domingo&#x2019;s Joe Jackson in &#x201C;Michael&#x201D; could earn him a fifth nomination after back-to-back bids for &#x201C;Rustin&#x201D; and &#x201C;Sing Sing.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Anne Hathaway is at the forefront with her Penelope in &#x201C;The Odyssey,&#x201D; while Samantha Morton also gives the epic another supporting contender. Pen&#xE9;lope Cruz is playing double duty this year, most likely to be recognized for &#x201C;The Invite,&#x201D; though also has a credible opportunity in &#x201C;La Bola Negra.&#x201D;

The latest news is that Amanda Seyfried is not eligible for SAG attention for her work in Nathan Fielder and Lance Oppenheim&#x2019;s documentary &#x201C;You Can See Everything.&#x201D; That could leave a spot open for Olivia Colman (&#x201C;Elsinore&#x201D;), Sandra H&#xFC;ller (&#x201C;Project Hail Mary&#x201D;), Kate O&#x2019;Flynn (&#x201C;Tender Loving Care&#x201D;) or Gemma Chan (&#x201C;Josephine&#x201D;).

In the TV race, it&#x2019;s likely that audiences will see a familiar cast taking the stage with Noah Wyle and his &#x201C;The Pitt&#x201D; crew, who took the prize last year. The show could go up some of the same players &#x2014; &#x201C;The Diplomat&#x201D; and &#x201C;Landman&#x201D; would be repeat noms from last year &#x2014; as well as others like &#x201C;Paradise,&#x201D; &#x201C;The Gilded Age&#x201D; and &#x201C;Slow Horses.&#x201D; As for a new edition eligible for the first time this season, &#x201C;Furious&#x201D; could make a big splash at the Actor Awards with excellent performances from both the lead and supporting casts.

In the comedy race, another Emmy repeat may be in place with Apple TV taking this award twice in a row &#x2014; last year for &#x201C;The Studio,&#x201D; this year could see &#x201C;Widow&#x2019;s Bay,&#x201D; which dominated the Emmys. &#x201C;Hacks&#x201D; will also be a huge contender for one last time, as will the usual suspects &#x201C;Abbott Elementary,&#x201D; &#x201C;Only Murders in the Building,&#x201D; &#x201C;Shrinking&#x201D; and possibly &#x201C;The Bear.&#x201D; That said, Apple also has &#x201C;Margo&#x2019;s Got Money Troubles&#x201D; and the return of &#x201C;Ted Lasso,&#x201D; both of which could steal away spots.

In comedy, Matthew Rhys is the early predicted nominee after his &#x201C;Widow&#x2019;s Bay&#x201D; success, but Jason Sudeikis re-enters the race in a category he&#x2019;s won twice for &#x201C;Ted Lasso.&#x201D; Plus, never count out Harrison Ford, one of the town&#x2019;s most beloved actors, for &#x201C;Shrinking.&#x201D; In drama, it&#x2019;s tough to imagine Wyle not taking it once again, but with supporting and lead together, some of his co-stars could go against him. Additions to this year&#x2019;s race could be Kyle Chandler and Aaron Pierre for &#x201C;Lanterns.&#x201D; And in limited, much like at the Emmys, expect multiple nods for &#x201C;DTF St. Louis,&#x201D; meaning David Harbour and Jason Bateman up against each other. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid3' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Jean Smart is a top contender for the last time in this category for &#x201C;Hacks,&#x201D; but unlike the Emmys, she hasn&#x2019;t always taken the trophy. &#x201C;Widow&#x2019;s Bay&#x2019;s&#x201D; Kate O&#x2019;Flynn is solidly in the race (and won the supporting Emmy), as is Lisa Kudrow, a two-time SAG winner returning with &#x201C;The Comeback.&#x201D; Two-time nominee Hannah Waddingham is back for &#x201C;Ted Lasso.&#x201D; The drama race could see a plethora of actresses from &#x201C;The Pitt&#x201D; in the race, as well as Keri Russell (&#x201C;The Diplomat&#x201D;), Carrie Coon (&#x201C;The Gilded Age&#x201D;), Zendaya (&#x201C;Euphoria&#x201D;) and Emmy Rossum for the only freshman show, &#x201C;Furious.&#x201D; In the limited/movie category, both Linda Cardellini (&#x201C;DTF St. Louis&#x201D;) and Sally Field (&#x201C;Remarkably Bright Creatures&#x201D;) took home Emmys, but keep an eye on Florence Pugh with her impressive role in &#x201C;East of Eden" and Meghann Fahy who shone in "The Good Daughter."

The latest way for comedians to find a second act: AI.

Buchwald has signed the estate of stand-up comedian Sam Kinison , who died at 38 in a 1992 car accident, to develop new business opportunities surrounding his name and likeness. Enter Kinison's AI avatar, powered by the AI platform Uare.AI. The company, founded by LivePerson founder Rob LoCascio, has developed a model of Kinison, which Buchwald says can be used to &#x201C;expand opportunities&#x201D; for the late comedian &#x201C;across multiple verticals.&#x201D; The agency is working with Kinison's brother and former manager, Bill Kinison, to figure out places the avatar could be deployed. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories '14th' Director Ava DuVernay on Midterm Elections: 'Either Way We're in Trouble' ‘Golden Girls’ and 'Gilmore Girls' Writers' 'Silver Foxes' Screenplay Acquired by Alder Street Productions (EXCLUSIVE)

&#x201C;Sam was always on the cutting-edge of comedy and entertainment, and with the genius of Uare.ai&#x2019;s work and the Buchwald agency&#x2019;s vision, we&#x2019;re keeping the promise of my brother&#x2019;s legacy alive,&#x201D; Bill Kinison said in a statement. &#x201C;I can&#x2019;t wait to see what Sam will do!&#x201D;

Kinison's style was associated with intense outbursts, screams and an acerbic delivery. He released five comedy albums throughout his career, winning a posthumous Grammy in 1994 for the album &#x201C;Live from Hell.&#x201D; He made numerous appearances on &#x201C;The Tonight Show Starring Johnny Carson,&#x201D; &#x201C;The Late Show with David Letterman&#x201D;&#xA0;and hosted &#x201C;Saturday Night Live&#x201D;&#xA0;in 1986. He also appeared in Rodney Dangerfield's film &#x201C;Back to School.&#x201D; After Kinison's 1992 death, celebrity tributes included a 1993 Fox special featuring appearances by Dangerfield, Robin Williams and Jim Carrey. Kinison was also repeatedly highly regarded by radio star Howard Stern. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The licensing of Kinison's AI avatar comes as celebrities, both living and dead, have found a new revenue stream by monetizing their name, voice and likeness through AI as the industry grapples with its ethical implications. Michael Caine joined the estates of Stan Lee and Judy Garland in licensing his voice to ElevenLabs, with their cloned voices available for commercial licensing and audiobook narration. The estate of Val Kilmer was also paid for allowing the late actor's likeness to appear in &#x201C;As Deep As the Grave,&#x201D; a film he was cast in but couldn't film due to his battle with throat cancer. He died in 2025. (The use of Kilmer's likeness also abided by SAG-AFTRA guidelines, the filmmakers told Variety this spring.)

More recently, &#x201C;The View&#x201D; co-host Sunny Hostin licensed her likeness this summer to the AI creative startup Fountain 0, weeks after Higgsfield licensed the appearances of the streamer N3on and UFC&#x2019;s Israel Adesanya and Quinton &#x2018;Rampage&#x2019; Jackson, among others, for its most recent film &#x201C;Cully Hill Boys.&#x201D;

Maleah Joi Moon didn&#x2019;t audition her way into Hillman College. Debbie Allen walked backstage at &#x201C;Hell&#x2019;s Kitchen,&#x201D; held the Tony winner&#x2019;s face in her hands and decided she had found the daughter of Whitley Gilbert and Dwayne Wayne.

&#x201C;She&#x2019;s never been apologetic about letting me know my light,&#x201D; Moon says of Allen, the choreographer, director and producer who shaped the original TV series &#x201C; A Different World &#x201D; and now shepherds Netflix &#x2019;s sequel comedy, which is eligible in this season&#x2019;s Golden Globes race. &#x201C;She&#x2019;s a tree to me, and I know that sounds kind of woo-woo, but it means she&#x2019;s so sturdy.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Gemma Chan Says She’d ‘Absolutely’ Play a Bond Girl Amid Fan-Casting: ‘I’m Flattered’ 'Unzipped' 4K Restoration to Make Streaming Debut on Criterion Channel (EXCLUSIVE)

The call came the weekend before Moon left the Alicia Keys musical. There was no Zoom or pleasantries. &#x201C;She gets straight to the point,&#x201D; Moon says.

Moon plays Deborah, the daughter of the sitcom&#x2019;s beloved couple; the casting carries a full-circle weight for her own family. Her mother immigrated from Belize, and her father grew up in the Bronx. Neither came from a world where kids went off to college, which is precisely why the original series hit so hard.

&#x201C;You see these young, Black, stylish, joyful, well-educated, pursuing academia young people and she had that same feeling that everybody else had in the world when they saw the 1980s version,&#x201D; says Moon.

Building Deborah started in the writers&#x2019; room, where showrunner Felicia Pride invited Moon to talk through her own life story. The first relationship she built was the one with Whitley. Rewatching Jasmine Guy&#x2019;s performance as an actor, not just as a fan, Moon found more than comic timing. &#x201C;I saw somebody who was strong-willed, somebody who was outspoken, ambitious and not afraid to be who she is, which is huge for a Black woman,&#x201D; she says. &#x201C;I know so much of who I am is my mom living inside of me.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Guy and Kadeem Hardison, back as Whitley and Dwayne, were generous with on-set wisdom. Hardison taught her to count her steps to her mark; Guy called and talked for two hours at a stretch. Both preach the same gospel: take care of yourself. &#x201C;When outside influences are coming in to say who they think you are,&#x201D; Moon says, &#x201C;[Guy] inspires me to remember who the fuck I am.&#x201D;

Moon, who is queer, is equally passionate about Amir, played by Jordan Herron Hall, the franchise&#x2019;s first openly queer character. She frames him as a person who happens to be queer rather than a queer character. &#x201C;Black love in all forms, in the sexuality sense, in the gender sense, in the community sense, in the familial sense, in the self-sense, is Black radicalism,&#x201D; she says. &#x201C;That is our game changer.&#x201D;

With a Tony and a Grammy already on the shelf, Moon is now focusing on music, her first love before acting or dance. She&#x2019;s been in the studio workshopping what her sound might be, and she&#x2019;s signed on to projects she can&#x2019;t yet name. A &#x201C;Hell&#x2019;s Kitchen&#x201D; film? She&#x2019;d audition for Keys all over again. A Broadway return? &#x201C;Hadestown,&#x201D; where her friend Amber Iman is currently starring, is on her wish list.

One piece of the Hillman inheritance is harder to celebrate. The original &#x201C;A Different World&#x201D; was born as a spinoff of &#x201C;The Cosby Show,&#x201D; and Moon doesn&#x2019;t pretend otherwise. &#x201C;We know that there is a complicated history. We&#x2019;re not going to beat around the bush,&#x201D; she says.

The two shows &#x201C;have their own fortitude, like they have their own legacies, both of them,&#x201D; Moon says. &#x201C;As much as they are interlinked, it&#x2019;s so wonderful that they both stand on their own.&#x201D;

Her prayer is that the Netflix version earns the same footing. &#x201C;No matter what that conversation looks like, the point is that we are telling a story of love that was born in its genesis from &#x2018;The Cosby Show&#x2019; and has continued through this generational re-embarking of another story and another story and another story,&#x201D; she says. &#x201C;That is how love is passed down. Period.&#x201D;

EXCLUSIVE: UTA has hired Sam Yabrow as a talent agent based in its Los Angeles office.

Yabrow joins from Buchwald, bringing nearly a decade of entertainment industry experience spanning casting and talent representation.

Clients expected to join him at UTA include Will Price ( The Only Living Pickpocket in New York , The Chair Company ), Igby Rigney ( The Shards ), Everett Blunck ( The Plague , The Audacity ) and Jaren Lewison ( Eternally Yours ).

Yabrow began his career in casting in New York before moving into talent representation at Abrams Artists Agency, later known as A3 Artists Agency. Following A3's closure in 2024, he joined Buchwald, where he spent the past two and a half years. He relocated to Los Angeles earlier this year. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

